    "created_at": "2016-10-28T14:15:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-28T14:15:03Z",
    "body": "I'm fine with using the target's Realm for the event, and think this is the sane thing to do.  In particular, that allows us to define behavior for all targets, not just nodes!\n\nI'm not fine with the way the tests are written in https://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/pull/4088/files because it presupposes a particular resolution of https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=20567. I would prefer those tests to actually compare the event's Realm to the target's Realm.  I'll comment in that PR.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
